# Shell scripts MUST check out with LF, on every platform.
#
# deployment/docker-entrypoint.sh is the image ENTRYPOINT. With core.autocrlf=true
# — the default on Git for Windows — a fresh clone rewrites it to CRLF, the
# shebang becomes `#!/bin/sh\r`, and the container dies at startup with the
# famously misleading:
#
#   exec /app/deployment/docker-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# Reproduced 2026-07-28 in a clean worktree on Windows. CI never catches this
# because it runs on ubuntu-latest, and an existing working tree never shows it
# because the file is already LF on disk — only new clones break.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else the image execs directly.
*.bash text eol=lf
